SEE CALLS HEALTH CAPTURES
BEGIN_TEXT
The radio listens by scanning: it visits each window of the scan plan in
turn and decodes every ALE call it hears. This screen shows what it is
doing now: scanning, holding on one window, recording, or taking a WWV
clock reading. INCOMING means a call to your own address was heard in the
last minute: the Calls screen says who and on which channel.

Channels are shown by name. A channel in your channel plan shows its
designator; one the scan plan labels shows that label; any other shows
its place in the scan plan, W2C1 for window 2, channel 1.

Hold, release, record and plan are orders to the scanner. It takes them
at its own pace, between visits: the screen shows "order pending" until
it has. Every hold and every recording ends by itself, after 15 minutes at
most. None of them transmits: the scanner only listens.

When the scanner isn't answering, the screen keeps what it last said, in
grey, and orders can't be given.
END
